    "content": "The 2026 Boston Marathon requires qualifying times ranging from 2:55:00 to 5:20:00 depending on age and gender (effective for 2026/2027 races). Registration is not guaranteed; due to high demand, a \"cut-off\" time is often applied, meaning runners may need to be several minutes faster than their standard (e.g., a 4:34 buffer for 2026).2026 & 2027 Boston Marathon Qualifying StandardsAge 18–34: Men 2:55:00 | Women/Non-Binary 3:25:00Age 35–39: Men 3:00:00 | Women/Non-Binary 3:30:00Age 40–44: Men 3:05:00 | Women/Non-Binary 3:35:00Age 45–49: Men 3:15:00 | Women/Non-Binary 3:45:00Age 50–54: Men 3:20:00 | Women/Non-Binary 3:50:00Age 55–59: Men 3:30:00 | Women/Non-Binary 4:00:00Age 60–64: Men 3:50:00 | Women/Non-Binary 4:20:00Age 65–69: Men 4:05:00 | Women/Non-Binary 4:35:00Age 70–74: Men 4:20:00 | Women/Non-Binary 4:50:00Age 75–79: Men 4:45:00 | Women/Non-Binary 5:05:00Age 80+: Men 5:00:00 | Women/Non-Binary 5:20:00Key DetailsCut-off Times: For the 2026 race, all runners needed to be 4 minutes and 34 seconds faster than the standard listed above.Age Requirement: Age is determined by your age on the day of the 2026 race.Eligibility: Times must be run on a certified course.Application: Applications are accepted over a one-week period in September for the following year's race.Downhill Courses: Note that courses with a net downhill elevation, such as Revel, have specific, separate rules for qualifying.Note: For the most up-to-date information, check the official B.A.A. website.",
